"Rahim and Ayesha were relay race partners on a running team. Rahim was able to run each mile twice as fast as Ayesha, but Ayesha was able to run twice as far as Rahim did. If Ayesha ran 4 miles and Rahim completed his part of the race in 16 minutes, how long in minutes did Ayesha take to complete her part?","Aaron and Vanessa were relay race partners on a running team. Aaron was able to run each mile twice as fast as Vanessa, but Vanessa was able to run twice as far as Aaron did. If Vanessa ran 4 miles and Aaron completed his part of the race in 16 minutes, how long in minutes did Vanessa take to complete her part?",64,64,64,64,"Let Ayesha’s speed be v miles per minute. Then Rahim’s speed is 2v (twice as fast).

Ayesha can run twice as far as Rahim. Given Ayesha ran 4 miles, Rahim ran 2 miles.

Rahim’s time = distance/speed = 2 miles / (2v) = 1/v minutes.
We’re told Rahim’s time is 16 minutes, so 1/v = 16 ⇒ v = 1/16 miles per minute.

Ayesha’s time = distance/speed = 4 miles / (1/16) = 64 minutes.

