Ali has four 10 taka notes and six 20 taka notes that he saved after working for Mr. Rahman on his rice field. Ali gives his sister half of the total money he has and uses 3/5 of the remaining amount of money to buy dinner. Calculate the amount of money he has after buying the dinner.,Ali has four $10 bills and six $20 bills that he saved after working for Mr. James on his farm. Ali gives her sister half of the total money he has and uses 3/5 of the remaining amount of money to buy dinner. Calculate the amount of money he has after buying the dinner.,32,32,32,32,"Step 1: Calculate Ali’s total money.
- Four 10 taka notes = 4 × 10 = 40 taka
- Six 20 taka notes = 6 × 20 = 120 taka
- Total = 40 + 120 = 160 taka

Step 2: Ali gives his sister half of the total.
- Half of 160 = 80 taka
- Remaining = 160 − 80 = 80 taka

Step 3: Ali uses 3/5 of the remaining to buy dinner.
- 3/5 of 80 = 48 taka
- Money left after dinner = 80 − 48 = 32 taka

