"Santiago loves to go swimming and has to swim across a 20-kilometer lake. He can swim at a pace of 2 kilometers per hour. He swims 60% of the distance. After that, he stops on an island and rests for half as long as the swimming time. He then finishes the remaining distance while going half the speed. How long did it take him to get across the lake?","James loves to go swimming and has to swim across a 20-mile lake. He can swim at a pace of 2 miles per hour. He swims 60% of the distance. After that, he stops on an island and rests for half as long as the swimming time. He then finishes the remaining distance while going half the speed. How long did it take him to get across the lake?",17,17,17,17,"Let's define the total distance and break the journey into parts.

- Total distance across the lake: 20 km
- Initial swimming speed: 2 km/h

Step 1: Swim 60% of the distance
- Distance = 60% of 20 km = 0.6 × 20 = 12 km
- Time = distance / speed = 12 / 2 = 6 hours

Step 2: Rest
- Rest time = half of swimming time = 0.5 × 6 = 3 hours

Step 3: Swim the remaining distance at half speed
- Remaining distance = 20 − 12 = 8 km
- New speed = half of 2 km/h = 1 km/h
- Time = 8 / 1 = 8 hours

Total time = swimming time (first part) + rest + swimming time (second part)
= 6 + 3 + 8 = 17 hours

